senses.gloss:
उत्-था (उद्-√ स्था, Pāṇ. viii, 4, 61; cf. उत्-तम्भ्, col. 1), P. Ā. (but not Ā. in the sense of ‘rising, standing up’, Pāṇ. i, 3, 24) -तिष्ठति, -ते (pf. -तस्थौ, aor. -अस्थात् &c.) to stand up, spring up, rise, raise one's self, set out, RV.; AV.; ŚBr.; Ragh.; Śak.; Bhag. &c.;
to rise (from the dead), BhP.;
to rise (from any occupation), leave off;
to finish, AitBr.; ŚBr.; TāṇḍyaBr. &c.;
to come forth, arise, appear, become visible, result;
to spring, originate from, RV.; AV.; ŚBr.; TS.; MBh.; Kathās. &c.;
to come in (as revenues), Śak.;
to rise (for the performance of any action);
to be active or brave;
to make efforts, take pains with, strive for;
to excel, MBh.; R. &c.:
Caus. -थापयति (aor. 1. sg. उ॑द्-अतिष्ठिपम्, AV. vii, 95, 2) to cause to stand up, raise, rouse, start, AV.; AitBr.; TBr.; ŚBr.; MBh.; Daś.; BhP. &c.;
to set up, lift up, erect, Gobh.; MBh.; R.; Hit. &c.;
to get out, Hit.;
to drive out, send out, push out, AitBr. : Kathās.; BhP.;
to excite;
to produce, Ragh.; Sāh.;
to arouse, awaken, raise to life, make alive, animate;
to stir up, agitate, ŚBr.; KauṣUp.; Hariv.; R.; Kathās. &c.:
Desid. -तिष्ठासति, to wish or intend to stand up, ŚBr. xi, 1, 6, 5;
to intend to leave off (a sacrifice), Nyāyam.
